WEBVTT

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.400
Okay! Let's start "Hayate No Gotoku!"

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.260
Tonight I, Chef Hayate Ayasaki,

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.660
will try to whip up a special curry dish

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.530
with summer veggies.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:11.240
Let's begin...

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.710
Hey, hey, Hayata-kun! Hayata-kun!

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.800
What is it, Segawa-san?

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.100
Is the curry gonna be spicy?

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.990
It'll have a kick to it.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.430
I can't eat spicy food! 
Could you make it mild?

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:28.250
Okay, I'll make it mild...

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:30.000
<i>Whoa, wait a sec!</i>

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.250
Curry has to be spicy.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.580
But I can't eat spicy food!

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.690
I'd rather have hayashi rice.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:39.760
Nobody asked what you wanted!

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.280
Let's do sushi instead. Sushi!

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.340
The fancy stuff! The really fancy stuff!

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.540
<i>What's sushi got to do with anything?</i>

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.170
Anything goes?

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.160
Then I want omelet rice.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.610
I'll start cooking some salisbury steaks.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.870
They'll be done in about 20 minutes.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:58.660
Don't cook whatever you want!

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.030
What about my curry?

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:01.940
And my sushi?

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:03.230
No sushi.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:12.050
Yes. I'm doing that, but...

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:20.050
What? Um, no... Please be patient.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:30.020
I, Ruri Tsugumi, will get...

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.340
...the black camellia.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:08.500
What do I need to do to get 
closer to my big sister?

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.880
Where'd you come from, Tsugumi-san?

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:14.960
I scaled the wall!

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.040
What are you, a cat?

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.880
I think it'll be difficult for 
you to get closer to her.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:24.920
Why? I'm so cute!

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:27.640
So cute! Cute! Cute!

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.720
You asked why it'll be difficult.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:31.230
Don't ignore my cuteness!

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:34.100
Miss Nagi has...

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:36.230
...no interest in you.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:39.920
She's improved in this regard,

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:42.490
but Miss Nagi still hates 
dealing with people.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:44.990
She doesn't even notice

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.810
people who don't interest her.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:54.510
<i>I couldn't care less if 
you're my sister or not.</i>

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:59.420
I get it. Then...

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:03.680
She'll become someone who'll interest me?

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.940
So she said. Then she 
scaled the wall and left.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:10.310
Is she a cat, or something?

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.660
As you said before,

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.950
I wonder what her agenda is.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:16.440
Why she wants to get closer to you.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:22.740
To be honest, I don't sense 
any malice from Tsugumi.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:26.240
But I do have a bad feeling.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.690
A bad feeling?

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:28.790
Yeah.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:33.080
I feel like I'm about to lose 
something really precious.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:36.500
Lose something... precious.

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:43.650
Everyone has something precious.

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:47.970
Something they love and long for.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:53.730
Something special that 
nothing else could replace.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:57.500
But when you try to protect 
this precious thing,

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:00.420
you end up losing something 
even more important.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.620
<b> New Century TV!* Social Media and TV Combined!!</b>

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:08.620
You want to become someone 
who'll interest Nagi?

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:11.710
Yes. You're my big 
sister's friend, right?

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:12.870
What can I do?

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:15.030
Let's see...

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:18.630
Maybe you can play video games with her.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:20.210
Video games?

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:24.470
 <i>Dondoko Quest VIII</i>

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:22.700
This just came out today.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.470
I bet she'd like it.

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:29.510
I'll take it home and play 
it with my big sister...

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:30.510
Wait, wait.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:32.140
What?

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.270
Pay up! It's 7,350 yen.

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.220
It's not free?

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:39.980
No, it's for sale.

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:41.990
Even though I'm a kid?

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:43.400
Doesn't matter.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:52.330
Can't I borrow it and return it later...

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.330
I said no!

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:58.590
<i>Don't lose heart now, Tsugumi.</i>

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:02.710
<i>If you can get closer to 
your sister for 7,350 yen...</i>

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:06.220
Okay, I'll take it!

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:07.840
Thank you!

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:13.960
Now I can get closer to my sister.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:16.980
Do you have the console?

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:20.590
Um, you are...

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:21.490
I'm Kayura.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:24.480
I live in the same apartment building. 
I'm friends with Nagi.

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:26.740
What console?

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:28.660
For the game.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:32.740
You need the corresponding 
console to play that game.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:36.450
What? How much is that?

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:38.710
About 20,000 yen.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:40.460
<b> Bank ATM</b>

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:40.460
<b>Avoid Excessive Use</b>

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:41.850
I'm set now, right?

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:44.570
Why are you getting mad at me?

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.140
One more thing...

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:47.210
What?

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:51.340
Another game came out today...

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.970
...that I think Nagi would like better.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:57.980
You think this one would be better 
to help me get closer to her?

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:58.910
Yup.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:02.980
Chiharu always recommends 
adventure games.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:03.940
Humph.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:10.960
But Nagi likes FPS games like this one.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:12.870
And how much is it?

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:15.120
6,800 yen.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:20.430
Thank you!

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:25.290
I didn't think I'd spend 
so much, but it's fine!

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:27.170
Now I can get closer to my sister...

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.400
Hey, Tsugumi-san.

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:32.590
Hayate Ayasaki!

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:36.100
Good timing. I finally did it.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:39.350
Oh, Miss Nagi already has those games.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.610
She said they were both crap.

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:48.560
I don't believe this!

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:52.490
That Nagi.

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:57.120
Calling a roleplaying game that's just a remake 
with nothing new a crappy game is fine...

00:07:57.690 --> 00:08:00.560
But to say that of the latest FPS,

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:02.750
one can only conclude it's an 
excuse for her sucking at it.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:04.910
What?

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:06.250
Um...

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:09.680
Well, maybe if you only read manga,

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:13.360
it would make you like high intensity stuff.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:18.480
All the light novels you read are 
full of nudity, Chiharu.

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:21.410
Why you!

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:23.590
Light novels are fine that way!

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:26.620
They're just printing 
what the readers demand.

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:29.400
Just responding to demands makes 
something worth producing?

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.900
Diversity is important!

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:34.890
I read all kinds of manga.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:36.910
Look at "Crimsons."

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:39.680
The main character is a salmon.

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:41.960
It makes you think.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:44.390
You're acting all literary now?

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:46.830
What? What's wrong 
with being literary?

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.770
What's important is the 
entertainment factor.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:52.280
The barometer is sales.

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:53.280
What?

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.480
Come on, you two.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:58.600
Don't get so upset.
It's only manga and light novels.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:01.060
"<i>Only</i>"?

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:04.140
You know, Nagi's the one 
 at fault here.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:05.360
I'm gonna let her have it!

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:06.810
Bring her over right now!

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:08.560
What?

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:14.290
<i>If this continues, I'll never 
get closer to my big sister.</i>

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:17.140
And?

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:18.530
What do you want?

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.490
Well...

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:22.790
It's about the games 
that came out today.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.000
Right, they're crap.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.540
Don't call them crap!

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.940
If you play to the end, 
they're kinda good...

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:30.820
I did play to the end.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:34.000
Don't lump me, Nagi Sanzenin,

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:35.550
in with your typical otaku.

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:39.260
Whether it's a video game, 
anime, or manga,

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:41.120
I only rate them after I've played,

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:43.060
watched, or read the entire thing!

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:49.440
Even though I might initially think, 
"Whoa, talk about a total letdown!"

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:54.240
I only call a game crap 
after I've finished it!

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:54.940
Whoa!

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:59.200
That's why I get the 
game the day before...

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.580
Skip school, stay home, fake illness,

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:05.040
stay up all night, and don't even bathe,

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:08.980
as I play continuously!

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:16.170
<i>Scum.</i>

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:18.930
<i>I kinda knew this, but...</i>

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.710
<i>She's such scum, it's almost refreshing.</i>

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:26.270
So that's why you didn't go 
to school yesterday or today?

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:27.290
Right.

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.560
Please go to school.

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:32.750
It's gonna be hard to 
get closer to this one.

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:37.080
I... I have to get closer to my big sister,

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:38.700
even if she's scum.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.450
What? Scum?

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.870
Did you just call me scum?

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.750
You did, didn't you? Didn't you?

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:46.160
I did not.

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:48.340
Humph. Whatever.

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:50.530
Since I'm here in Akiba,

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:52.630
I'll get something and go home.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.460
What are you getting?

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:59.550
Hm, I think I'll go look there.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:03.470
<b>Connecting</b>

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:03.470
<b>Theater</b>

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:03.470
<b>Part A</b>

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:06.720
Fumi-chan. Say "pizza" ten times.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:09.050
Okay! Pizza, pizza, pizza, pizza, pizza,

00:11:09.050 --> 00:11:10.980
pizza, pizza, pizza, pizza, pizza.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:12.480
And what's this?

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:13.800
Tempest.

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:18.190
Wrong! It's your elbow, 
 but whoa! Tempest?

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:22.660
<b>Connecting</b>

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:22.660
<b>Theater</b>

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:22.660
<b>Part B</b>

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.950
Isumi-san. Say "pizza" ten times.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:29.370
Okay. Pizza, pizza, 
pizza, pizza, pizza,

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.330
pizza, pizza, pizza, pizza, pizza.

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:32.960
And another ten times.

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:34.800
Pizza, pizza, pizza, pizza...

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:35.730
Faster!

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:36.540
Pizza, pizza...

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:37.530
Enunciate!

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:38.460
Pizza, pizza, pi...

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:43.180
Where are we?

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:47.180
It's a used PC and game store.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:50.960
I've been thinking lately

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:53.300
that I need to play old games

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:57.190
to really grasp the history of it all.

00:11:57.830 --> 00:11:59.280
Like... this.

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:01.160
"Silver Ghost."

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:04.570
It's a simulation roleplaying 
game from the '80s.

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:08.310
Usually roleplaying 
games have like, what,

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:09.850
four characters in the main party?

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:12.580
Or they're just all in a horse carriage.

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:14.290
Uh, yeah.

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:20.210
But here you can have 15 characters 
walk together, all lined up.

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:24.220
I like the slow, bit-by-bit action.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:26.980
I think it's cute.

00:12:26.980 --> 00:12:29.720
Huh? I see.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.550
I've been thinking I want to play these

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:33.730
to understand the 
history of video games.

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:37.050
Take the PC version of the game "Ys II."

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:39.580
The instructions were written

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:42.570
by the guy who wrote "Fortune Quest"!

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:46.070
It's an excellent game that can be 
enjoyed for the reading as well.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:51.830
<b> 6F Software
5F Girls' Doujin
4F Guys' Doujin
3F Manga</b>

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:56.500
I wish they'd release more 
old anime on Blu-ray.

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:59.250
Like Gowappa 5.

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:02.760
What's this awkward robot?

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:04.010
How dare you!

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:08.820
This is Gordam, the 
heavy-duty robot goliath

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:11.680
that the Gowappa members 
ride in Gowappa 5.

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:17.240
It's groundbreaking because the robot 
can barely move any of its joints.

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:19.190
Then how does it fight?

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:21.300
He's super strong!

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.240
He crushes enemies one by one

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:26.080
even though his joints barely move!

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:27.450
I see.

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:36.510
Even though she's useless as a human,
her eyes are lighting up...

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:39.700
Well, she really loves this stuff.

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:41.380
No, Nagi.

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:44.720
Wh-What do you mean, Kayura?

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:48.250
There's a Gowappa 5 DVD box set.

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:50.970
So there's not much point in a Blu-ray.

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:55.830
More importantly, when's the DVD for 
"Laserion" gonna be released?

00:13:55.830 --> 00:14:00.110
It's not in "Super Robot Wars" either! 
And what about "GoLion"?!

00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:07.430
Well, who cares about those?

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:11.690
It doesn't do any good 
to watch old anime.

00:14:11.690 --> 00:14:13.560
Why you!

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:16.000
Apologize to the God of Anime!

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.850
Don't shun those shows just 
because you don't like them!

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:20.890
They're into the same things...

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:23.130
so why can't they get along?

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.730
Deeply sinful, indeed.

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:30.940
If you find something both of you like...

00:14:30.940 --> 00:14:33.060
...then you might be able to be friends.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:35.980
Of course! That's a good idea.

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:39.690
So tell me, which one is good?

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:44.610
What, me? Um...

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:49.070
I'll show you a cute 
anime that I like:

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:50.950
The original "Minky Momo" series.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.590
This one.

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:54.700
Oh! It's so cute!

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:55.980
Right?

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:58.640
Or, for an old standby, there's 
 "Space Runaway Ideon."

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:01.210
Something newer would 
be "Madoka Magica."

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:04.770
And "Dog of Flanders" is also good.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:06.050
Uh huh.

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:08.500
And...

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:12.400
The anime Hayate-kun is recommending...

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:15.520
are all ones where the main 
character dies at the end.

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:17.450
Is he okay?

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:20.740
I'll take em' all!

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:22.350
Please!

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:25.020
That'll be 123,000 yen.

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:38.660
Um, how about we spread 
that over 24 payments.

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:40.620
<i>Are you trying to go 
into credit card debt?!</i>

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:45.030
Wait! You're going too far.

00:15:45.030 --> 00:15:49.760
But if I don't do this, I'll never 
get closer to you, big sister.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:53.920
Just buying everything you're 
told to isn't the way to go.

00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:55.720
Think! There are other ways.

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:57.970
B-But...

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:00.150
Besides, don't you think I like

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:02.690
things besides video games and anime?

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:05.060
Like what?

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:08.250
Um... Well,

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:10.360
like manga.

00:16:10.630 --> 00:16:12.860
<i>It's the same thing!</i>

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:16.640
Right. Manga is cheaper 
and easier to get hold of.

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:19.240
Which manga should I read first?

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:28.750
<i>Oh dear. We've just
 flipped a weird switch.</i>

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:32.490
What to read first?

00:16:32.490 --> 00:16:34.010
Well, that's a given.

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:35.940
Of course.

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:37.680
Yes...

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.390
<b>Doujinshi Game</b>

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.390
<b>Comic V</b>

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.390
Tachibana

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.390
<b>Please visit</b>

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.390
<b>{mic} V Tachibana</b>

00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:43.770
Sigh. I'm so bored.

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:47.110
Welcome!

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:49.220
Oh, it's you guys.

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:51.370
Hey, Wataru-san and Saki-san.

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:52.610
Long time no see.

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:57.430
Listen, Tsugumi. The thing 
you should start with is...

00:16:57.430 --> 00:16:59.740
Hey, it's the Jump manga!

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:01.450
Cuuuuuut!

00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:02.660
Ow!

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.620
Don't worry about famous titles.

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:08.920
Millions of others 
have already read those.

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:10.670
I'm sorry...

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:11.570
Listen up.

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:17.430
The series that all manga 
lovers must read first is...

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:22.520
<b>Hoero Pen</b>

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:22.520
...all 100-plus volumes by 
Kazuhiko Shimamoto!

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:26.150
Yikes, 100 volumes? 
That's not easy.

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:28.840
I'm still talking! 
Shut up and listen!

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:30.150
Y-Yes!

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:31.250
Listen.

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:35.470
<b>Hoero Pen</b>

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:32.730
The core of what makes

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.470
manga fun is found in all 
of Shimamoto's work.

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:37.300
Pay special attention to 
"Hoero Pen," and the

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:40.780
previous work, "Moeyo Pen," 
is even more indispensable.

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:42.540
But!

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:45.050
This is what many people miss.

00:17:45.050 --> 00:17:47.030
The new version of "Moeyo 
Pen" doesn't have

00:17:47.030 --> 00:17:49.920
the live action parts like the 
Bamboo Comics version.

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:53.370
But the Bamboo version 
lacks the postscript.

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:54.010
So...

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:57.470
If you want to read the 
complete "Moeyo Pen,"

00:17:57.470 --> 00:18:00.870
you have to read both the new version

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:03.770
and the Bamboo Comics version!

00:18:04.070 --> 00:18:06.850
Sorry, we don't carry either.

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:11.270
You idiot!

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:13.730
You call yourself a bookstore?

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:15.610
Get them!

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:18.830
You made a mistake, Nagi.

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:19.530
What?

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:25.290
Shimamoto's masterpiece is 
"Nine in Adversity"!

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:28.760
Equally satisfying is the world's 
first Original Laserdisc Anime

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:32.420
"Honoo No Tenkousei!"

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:36.300
Sorry, I don't carry them, either.

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:42.550
Why? They've been made 
into a movie and an anime!

00:18:44.710 --> 00:18:46.540
I told you two...

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:50.730
If you're to read anything, 
it's "Honoo No Ninja Man."

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:53.490
That exists?

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:56.990
What? Of course it does!
It's one of his best!

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.740
I can't believe you haven't read it!

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:02.380
Didn't it get canceled in 
the weekly comics?

00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:05.200
So what if the readers of 
Shonen Sunday didn't get it?

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.120
You've heard of it!

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:08.750
Never mind that. You have 
to read "Aoi Honoo."

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:11.440
That's too famous.

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.360
Shimamoto's stuff is more...

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:14.620
I just want you to know

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:17.100
that we don't have 
"Ninja Man" or "Aoi Honoo."

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:18.760
Order them!

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:18.760
<i>Disgraceful.</i>

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:23.150
How can they fight 
 over the same artist?

00:19:23.150 --> 00:19:24.760
Good question.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:27.900
Cashier

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:30.640
<i>New doujinshi
 arriving daily</i>

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:26.420
You know what?

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:28.390
I'm gonna find one that I like.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:30.640
Good idea.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:33.720
Hm, which one?

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:35.900
Oh! They're really colorful.

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:38.780
Excuse me, but that's...

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:43.990
There's lot of thin books here.

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:43.990
<b>Adult Area</b>
This area is for adults only. 
Must be over 18 to purchase items beyond this point.

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:47.040
Why don't you guys carry more

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:50.040
of Shimamoto's works?

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:51.170
Um...

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:52.670
What's wrong?

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:57.280
Um, the little girl just wandered...

00:19:57.280 --> 00:19:59.500
...into the thin books.

00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:00.760
What?

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:02.670
I tried to stop her.

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:05.930
No! Even I'm too 
young to read that stuff!

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.180
Tsugumi's way too young!

00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:14.040
I think I saw this book in 
my big sister's room.

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:15.190
I'll definitely get this one.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:16.900
And...

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:19.250
Tsugumi!

00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:21.680
You can't go...

00:20:24.170 --> 00:20:28.700
<b> No Under 18</b>

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:31.220
Tsu-Tsugumi?

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:34.670
I... I don't care, but...

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:36.420
...is this what...

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:39.420
...otaku are into?

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:43.030
Um, no! Well, maybe, yes.

00:20:43.030 --> 00:20:45.640
I-It's a misunderstanding! 
Or maybe not...

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:48.690
You're definitely losing 
your dignity as a big sister.

00:20:48.690 --> 00:20:50.720
What's that?

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:53.730
Oh, all right. I'll take one.

00:20:54.340 --> 00:20:56.980
Thank you!

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:59.290
Hey, Tsugumi-san.

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:02.400
Do you know the author 
of this doujinshi?

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:03.460
No.

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:06.990
But I read it in my sister's room

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:08.740
 30 Days Of Soul Burning

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:08.740
and I thought it was good.

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:11.950
Why? Is the author famous?

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:13.900
Uh huh. Uh huh.

00:21:13.900 --> 00:21:15.220
Well...

00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:16.580
Yes! Right!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.970
That's exactly what's 
special about that!

00:21:21.970 --> 00:21:24.580
Come over right now and I'll give you

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:26.630
a special look at my prized collection!

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:30.860
That author... might have a 
bestselling manga one day.

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:31.730
Huh?

00:23:05.220 --> 00:23:08.910
These salisbury steaks topped 
with grated daikon are so tasty.

00:23:08.910 --> 00:23:11.940
They're even good
 with demi-glace sauce.

00:23:11.940 --> 00:23:14.870
Anything that's made 
with love is delicious.

00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:16.850
That's right.

00:23:16.850 --> 00:23:19.760
Everyone has different tastes.

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:22.390
What's important is the 
love that's put into it.

00:23:22.390 --> 00:23:24.250
We have different opinions,

00:23:24.250 --> 00:23:27.260
but that's just the flip side of love.

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:30.900
Is this some kind of weird, 
 lightly veiled commentary

00:23:30.900 --> 00:23:33.480
about this week's episode?

00:23:33.480 --> 00:23:35.490
Um... No!

00:23:35.490 --> 00:23:37.290
Ow, ow, ow!

00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:38.970
Look forward to the next episode!
